## Refactor proposal for `src/Card.tsx`

Current shape: a single `<div>` with inline styles, raw hex/rgb literals, fixed pixel widths, and a click handler with no a11y affordances. All three findings trace back to the inline-style block plus the click on a non-semantic element.

### Proposed code

```tsx
// src/Card.tsx
import styles from "./Card.module.css";

type CardProps = {
  children: React.ReactNode;
  onActivate?: () => void;
};

export function Card({ children, onActivate }: CardProps) {
  const Root = onActivate ? "button" : "div";
  return (
    <Root
      type={onActivate ? "button" : undefined}
      onClick={onActivate}
      className={styles.card}
    >
      <div className={styles.body}>{children}</div>
      <aside className={styles.sidebar}>sidebar</aside>
    </Root>
  );
}
```

```css
/* src/Card.module.css */
.card {
  width: 100%;
  max-width: 50rem;            /* was width: 800px */
  padding: var(--space-3);     /* was padding: 24 */
  background: var(--color-surface-accent);  /* was #ff00aa */
  color: var(--color-text);                 /* was #0a0a0a */
  border: 1px solid var(--color-border);    /* was #cccccc */
  box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm);             /* was 0 2px 4px rgb(0,0,0) */
  outline-color: var(--color-focus);        /* was #1a73e8 */
  container-type: inline-size;
}

.body { font-size: clamp(0.95rem, 1.2vw, 1.125rem); }   /* was 18px fixed */
.sidebar { font-size: 0.875rem; color: var(--color-text-muted); }

@container (min-width: 40rem) {
  .card { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 15rem; gap: var(--space-3); }
}
```

### How each change maps to a finding

| Finding | Change |
|---|---|
| **`design_token_escape`** (crime_00002) | All nine raw color/shadow/px literals move out of inline `style={}` into a CSS module that consumes design tokens (`--color-*`, `--space-*`, `--shadow-*`). Agents editing the file can no longer copy a hex forward — there are no hexes to copy. |
| **`accessible_interaction_risk`** (crime_00001) | The clickable outer element becomes a real `<button>` when `onActivate` is provided. That gives keyboard focus, Enter/Space activation, and the right role for free — no `role="button"` + `tabIndex={0}` + `onKeyDown` patchwork needed. If the wrapper is non-interactive, it renders as `<div>` with no click handler. |
| **`responsive_fragility`** (crime_00003) | Fixed `width: 800px` / `720px` become `width: 100%; max-width: 50rem` so the card collapses below the breakpoint. The `18px` font scales via `clamp()`. The inner two-column layout is driven by a **container query** instead of a viewport media query, so a Card placed in a narrow column also collapses correctly. |

### Trade-offs worth flagging

- **Token names are illustrative.** This fixture has no design system; in a real repo I'd grep for the existing token source (Tailwind config, CSS vars, a `theme.ts`) before naming variables. If there's no system yet, that's a separate finding worth raising before the inline styles get fixed.
- **`onActivate` rename.** Renaming `onClick` → `onActivate` at the API surface is a small breaking change for callers but signals "this fires on click *and* keyboard activation," which is what a button actually does. If you'd rather preserve the prop name, keep `onClick` — the semantics still come out right because it's wired to a real `<button>`.
- **Container queries** need a fairly modern target (Safari 16+, baseline 2023). If the project still supports older browsers, fall back to a `@media (min-width: 40rem)` query on the parent.
